 "result_text": "Equation fields now use Knack's own formatted value for `.formatted`, so the days-vs-seconds case from the issue should come out as Knack shows it (4 instead of 372171.318\u2026). The raw value is still kept in `.raw`. I haven't run the code or any tests, and I didn't try it against a real Knack app.\n\n- **`knackpy/models.py`:** I added `equation` to `FIELD_SETTINGS` with `use_knack_format: True`, the same way `timer` and `name` already work. The default formatter then runs on Knack's formatted value rather than the raw one.\n- **`knackpy/fields.py`:** the check for whether a Knack-formatted value exists was a truthiness test. A formatted value of `0` would have fallen back to the raw value, which matters for equation fields. It now tests `is not None`. This also changes `name` and `timer` fields slightly: an empty-string formatted value is now passed to their formatter instead of being replaced by the raw value.",
